## Extending our capabilities

Evaluate patterns in wood grain to identify use as chimpanzee pounding tools!

```{r}
#| message: false
#| warning: false
#| echo: false
library(raster)
library(imager)
library(shotGroups)
convRas<-function(x) { if (x=="#FFFFFF") {1} else{0}}
fpath <-"woodgrain3.jpg"
image<- load.image(fpath)
image<-grayscale(image)
plot(image)
```

## Extending our capabilities

Evaluate patterns in wood grain to identify use as chimpanzee pounding tools!

```{r}
library(imager)
#get image dimensions (in pixels)
w<-width(image)
h<-height(image)
#canny edges (higher alpha = stricter acceptance threshold)
edges<-cannyEdges(image,alpha=0.8) 
plot(edges)
```

